WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
Your inbox already has the lead.

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Iris handles the admin around it.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Every new email is sorted by what it needs.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:12.000
A property answer, a showing request, a seller inquiry, a follow-up, or a person.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:23.000
When a buyer asks about a home, the draft includes the actual listing, price, photos, key details, and the next useful step, not a generic response.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.000
Broader searches get relevant options.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:31.000
Seller inquiries get one focused question and evaluation path.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Showing requests get real availability.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Sensitive, unclear, or high-stakes messages are flagged for review instead of being sent.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Your team chooses draft-only or approved auto-send rules.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.000
Iris remembers the thread, keeps lead details current, and follows up without losing the conversation.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.000
Open Gmail. Review what matters.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:59.520
Send better replies while the rest of the inbox stays organized.
